<title>LUXEMBOURG: SAFRA REPORTS 17 PCT 1996 PROFIT RISE.</title>
<headline>SAFRA REPORTS 17 PCT 1996 PROFIT RISE.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in million U.S. dlrs unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			189.8	     vs 162.1</p>
<p> Net per share		  10.78	     vs 9.16</p>
<p> Dividend per share	   4.50		vs 3.50</p>
<p> Total assets		   17,223.4	  vs 15,660.5</p>
<p> Net interest income	  266.2	     vs 235.4</p>
<p> Net commission income	79.8		vs 69.8</p>
<p> Credit loss provision	12.0		vs 1.0</p>
<p> Non-performing assets	15.4		vs 19.1</p>
<p>Quarter ending December 31, 1996</p>
<p> Group net			51.2		vs 42.1</p>
<p> Net per share		  2.91		vs 2.39</p>
<p>Note - Per share dividend figure for 1996 is before taking into account a planned two-for-one share split.</p>
<p>Safra is the holding company for five wholly-owned banks active in international private and commercial banking. The banks operate under the name of Republic National Bank of New York and are located in Switzerland, Luxembourg, France, Guernsey and Gibraltar. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
